msgstr ""

#.  Removed "all"
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Woodland Folk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:111
msgid ""
"Due to living amongst the forests of Loren Wood Elf infantry does not suffer "
"the usual −1 Command penalty when within woodland."
msgstr ""

#
#
#
#. 2: "2" missing
#. 3: Spelling Armour, Spelling Waywatchers, infiltration
#. 6: Spelling its
#. 7: Spelling penalty
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[glade-guard,†1]]1. Glade Guard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:130
msgid ""
"Wood Elves are just as famed for their bow as their High Elf cousins, and as "
"such Glade Guard units add +1 to their dice roll when making shooting "
"attacks. Therefore these units score a hit against targets in the open on a "
"3+, against defended targets on a 4+, and against fortified targets on a 5+."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wardancers,†2]]2. Wardancers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:135
msgid ""
"Wardancer stands are not deployed as independent units. Instead, any Glade "
"Guard or Eternal Guard unit may add one stand of Wardancers. This brings the "
"size of the unit to 4 stands – 3 regular stands plus the Wardancers stand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:139
msgid ""
"Wardancers always have the same Armour value as the rest of their unit. They "
"fight as part of their unit and can be removed as a unit casualty if the "
"player wishes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:143
msgid ""
"Wardancers casualties never count for Command penalties.  Wardancers stands "
"never cause the parent unit to be in Irregular Formation no matter how they "
"are placed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[waywatchers,†3]]3. Waywatchers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Famous for their bow skills even by a Wood Elf standards, Waywatchers shoot "
"the enemy with terrifying accuracy. They add +1 to their dice roll when "
"making shooting attacks and these attacks are resolved at −1 Armour value of "
"the enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:172
msgid ""
"Waywatchers can also ambush. Individual units can be infiltrated onto the "
"battlefield once the game has begun. To infiltrate a unit, the Wood Elf "
"player nominates the point where he wants the Waywatchers to appear and "
"issues an ‘infiltration’ order from any character. The character does not "
"have to be within his normal command range to issue an infiltration order – "
"the character’s command range is considered to extend over the entire "
"tabletop when issuing an infiltration order. Treat the order as issued to "
"the nominated point, and apply any modifiers for distance and proximity of "
"enemy, but ignore penalties of dense terrain. The nominated point must lie "
"either on the table within dense terrain or on any base edge other than the "
"enemy player’s own table edge. If successful, place one stand on the "
"nominated spot and arrange the rest of the unit around it. The infiltrated "
"unit cannot be placed so that it touches an enemy unit. Once deployed, "
"orders can be given to the unit by the same character that gave the "
"infiltration order if he is within his normal command range, the "
"infiltrating unit is considered to have used its first order to deploy. If "
"the infiltration order is failed the unit is not deployed and cannot "
"infiltrate that turn, it can attempt to infiltrate in a subsequent turn at "
"the same of a different place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:173
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[forest-spirits,†4]]4. Forest Spirits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:176
msgid ""
"Forest Spirits are woodland creatures. They are immune to terror and suffer "
"a −1 Command penalty when being ordered by General or Noble."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:177
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[wild-riders,†5]]5. Wild Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Wild Riders receive +1 Attack in the first round of every combat when "
"fighting to the front."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warhawk-riders,†6]]6. Warhawk Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:186
msgid ""
"Warhawk Riders can fly. They have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° "
"vision – stands in this unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the "
"purpose of evading and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. "
"Note that this unit still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge "
"an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[treeman,†7]]7. Treeman"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:190
msgid ""
"A Treeman can enter woods and suffers no command penalty for being within "
"the woods but cannot get defended status there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:192
msgid "A Treeman causes terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[treeman-ancient,†8]]8. Treeman Ancient"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:195
msgid ""
"The Treeman Ancient has a −1 Command penalty when issuing orders to units "
"other than Forest Spirits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:197
msgid ""
"The Treeman Ancient can join only Forest Spirit units and is able to cast "
"the <<tree-singing>> spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:199
msgid "Units joined by Treeman Ancient cause terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:201
msgid "The Treeman Ancient cannot be given any magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:204
msgid "There can only ever be one Treeman Ancient in any Wood Elf army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:205
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[branchwraith,†9]]9. Branchwraith"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:207
msgid ""
"A Branchwraith has a −1 Command penalty when issuing orders to units other "
"than Forest Spirits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:210
msgid ""
"A Branchwraith can join only Forest Spirit units and is able to cast the "
"<<tree-singing>> spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:213
msgid "A Branchwraith cannot be given any magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:214
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[giant-stag,†10]]10. Giant Stag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:216
msgid "Generals, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride a Giant Stag."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:218
msgid "The Stag adds +1 Attack to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:219
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[unicorn,†11]]11. Unicorn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:220
msgid "This mount can be ridden only by a Spell Weaver."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:222
msgid "The Unicorn adds +1 Attack to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:227
msgid ""
"Once per battle the Unicorn’s magical power adds +1 to the dice when casting "
"a spell. The player must announce that the Unicorn’s magic [.edit]#is being "
"used# before rolling to see if the spell works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:230
msgid "There can be only one Unicorn in the army."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:231
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warhawk,†12]]12. Warhawk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:233
msgid "General, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride a Warhawk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:236
msgid ""
"The Warhawk can fly, increasing its rider’s move from 60cm to 100cm, and it "
"adds +1 Attack to those of its rider."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[forest-dragon,†13]]13. Forest Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:239
msgid "Generals, Nobles and Spell Weavers may ride Forest Dragons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:246
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wood Elf spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree Singing"
msgstr ""

#.  Spelling their, force → forth, form → from
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:256
msgid ""
"_The Spell Weaver calls forth a mass of tangling branches to surround their "
"troops, protecting them from harm._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:262
msgid ""
"This spell may be cast upon a single unengaged friendly Infantry unit within "
"range, regardless of whether the caster can see them or not. The spell lasts "
"until the start of the caster’s next turn, or until the target unit moves in "
"any way. The target Infantry unit counts as Defended, even if it is in open "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twilight Host"
msgstr ""

#.  weird → eldritch, target unit → silent elves.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:270
msgid ""
"_An [.edit]#eldritch# enchantment forms around the [.edit]#silent elves#._"
msgstr ""

#.  next rearranged, magic → shooting
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:273
msgid ""
"The target unit causes terror until the next Wood Elf [.edit]#Shooting# "
"phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call of the Hunt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:282
msgid ""
"_The Spell Weaver’s voice sings out across the battlefield directing troops "
"above the tumult of combat with the magical Call of the Hunt._"
msgstr ""

#.  Add "The [enemy] unit"
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:287
msgid ""
"[.edit]#The target# unit may make a charge move into contact with the "
"nearest visible enemy unit in the same way as when charging. The enemy unit "
"may not shoot at the chargers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:289
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fury of the Forest"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:296
msgid ""
"_Trees shake, branches lash out and vines entangle the foe as they approach "
"the forest._"
msgstr ""

#.  Add "the", "the"
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:301
msgid ""
"The spell makes three shooting attacks on all enemy units within 10cm of the "
"chosen wooded terrain piece. Units get no armour save if within wooded "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/wood-elves.adoc:306
msgid ""
"Unengaged units are not driven back by this spell (the assault comes form "
"the ground beneath their feet). Engaged units carry over any hits scored "
"into the first round of combat; any hits scored count as having been struck "
"in the combat itself."
msgstr ""
